Redact rejected extra-field keys instead of echoing them

The extra_forbidden branch of summarize_validation_error still copied the
provider-supplied key from error['loc'] into the summary (up to the 60-char
cap), so short rogue keys — or a truncated prefix of a long one — could leak
reviewed-spec content into the LLMError message and logs.

Replace the rejected key with a fixed "<extra field>" placeholder for
extra_forbidden errors, keeping any leading schema path for context. The length
cap stays as a defensive backstop for unusually long legitimate schema paths
(now covered by a direct unit test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
